  "content": "<html><body><div><div class=\"single-box clearfix entry-content\">\n<p><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643028\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_01.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_01.jpg\"/></p>\n<p>When Waugh Thistleton Architects and Mithun sat down to design Bevel, the brief was as clear as it was ambitious: build an office tower in Bellevue, Washington, that challenges how North America thinks about commercial construction. The result is a 12-storey, 55-meter mass timber building developed by Skanska that, upon completion in August 2026, will claim the title of the tallest mass timber commercial office building on the continent.</p>\n<p>That distinction matters. While tall timber has appeared in multifamily housing and student accommodations across North America, no commercial office building has yet pushed through the boundaries of Type IVB construction code. Bevel does exactly that, and in doing so, it draws a new line in the sand for what sustainable workplace design can look like at scale.</p>\n<p>Designer: <a href=\"https://waughthistleton.com/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Waugh Thistleton Architects</a> and Mithun</p>\n<p><noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643029\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_02.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_02.jpg\"/></noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643029\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_02.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_02.jpg\"/></p>\n<p><noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643031\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_04.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_04.jpg\"/></noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643031\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_04.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_04.jpg\"/></p>\n<p>The building\u2019s structural logic is unapologetic about what it\u2019s made of. Mass timber columns, beams, and ceilings are left fully exposed throughout every office floor and across the ground-floor public areas. There\u2019s no cladding to soften or conceal the material \u2014 the timber is the experience. Paired with full-height perimeter windows and floor-to-ceiling glazing in the lobby, the building pulls natural light and the Pacific Northwest landscape into nearly every corner of its 18,580 square meters.</p>\n<p>Biophilic design threads through the project at every scale. The ground floor opens into a nature-infused lobby, native landscaping wraps the site, and the streetscape around Bevel expands with wider sidewalks and improved pedestrian connections that weave the building into Bellevue\u2019s downtown grid. It\u2019s a rare office project that considers what it does to the city around it, not just the tenants inside it.</p>\n<p><noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643032\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_05.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_05.jpg\"/></noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643032\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_05.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_05.jpg\"/></p>\n<p><noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643033\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_06.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_06.jpg\"/></noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643033\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_06.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_06.jpg\"/></p>\n<p>Given the region\u2019s seismic demands, Bevel\u2019s mass timber sits above grade while a steel core and lateral system handle structural resilience, and a concrete parking structure anchors the base below grade. It\u2019s a practical acknowledgment of the Pacific Northwest\u2019s geology \u2014 not a compromise, but a considered hybrid that makes the timber possible at this height.</p>\n<p>The certifications Bevel is targeting reflect the full breadth of that ambition: LEED v4 Platinum, Fitwel 2-Star, and Salmon-Safe. Stormwater capture and reuse systems, full electrification, and biodiversity-focused site design round out a sustainability stack that positions the building for long-term performance rather than just a headline at opening.</p>\n<p><noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643030\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_03.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_03.jpg\"/></noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643030\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_03.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_03.jpg\"/></p>\n\n<p><noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643034\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_07.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_07.jpg\"/></noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643034\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_07.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_07.jpg\"/></p>\n<p>This is also the first collaboration between London-based Waugh Thistleton and West Coast firm Mithun \u2014 two studios whose combined research in mass timber and workplace design across two continents makes Bevel feel like a genuinely global answer to a very local question: what should the next generation of office buildings be built from? The answer, it turns out, is wood.</p>\n<p><noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643035\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_08.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_08.jpg\"/></noscript><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-643035\" data-jpibfi-post-excerpt=\"\" data-jpibfi-post-title=\"Bevel Is Set to Become the Tallest Mass Timber Office Building in North America\" data-jpibfi-post-url=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/2026/08/21/bevel-is-set-to-become-the-tallest-mass-timber-office-building-in-north-america/\" data-jpibfi-src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_08.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.yankodesign.com/images/design_news/2026/08/bevel/bevel_yanko_design_08.jpg\"/></p>\n\n</div>\n</div></body></html>",
